<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia raises internal coffee price to new high.</title>
<headline>Colombia raises internal coffee price to new high.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's National Coffee Growers' Federation raised the country's internal coffee price to a new all-time high of 374,000 pesos per 125-kg load in the 10th such price hike since Jan. 31, a federation spokeman said.</p>
<p>The new price, up 8.2 percent from 345,625 pesos per load set on April 18, was based on an average price over the past week of $2.20 per pound for Colombian coffee in New York, the spokesman said.  </p>
<p>The internal price, which is set every Friday, has been cut just twice since the end of January when the federation introduced a new &quot;sliding scale&quot; formula to help bring it closer into line with world market prices.</p>
<p>((-- Juan Guillermo Londono, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
